WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.930
Litres and millilitres

2
00:00:01.930 --> 00:00:32.815
Namaste! Aaj ka lesson hai Litres and millilitres. Ek litre mein 1000 millilitres hote hain; bottle ki capacity isi relation se samjho. Is baat ko dheere-dheere samjhenge, phir ek aasaan example dekhenge. Learning mein galti hona bilkul normal hai; hum har step ko dobara check kar sakte hain.

3
00:00:32.815 --> 00:01:03.056
500 mL ki do bottles milkar 1 litre banti hain. Dhyaan do ki example mein kaunsi cheez badal rahi hai aur kaunsi same rehti hai. Pehle apna andaaza bolo, phir reason dhoondo. Agar tum kisi dost ko samjha sakte ho, to concept aur mazboot ho jaata hai.

4
00:01:03.056 --> 00:01:41.019
Paani ke bina measuring cup ki markings dekho aur 250 mL ke chaar equal pours draw karo. Apne observation ko ek sentence mein likho. Har number ya label ke saath sahi unit ya naam lagao. Sawaal solve karte waqt jaldi mat karo; clue ko underline karo, apna tareeka chuno, aur aakhir mein jawab ko example ke saath compare karo.

5
00:01:41.019 --> 00:02:56.300
Ab practice karo: 1 litre mein kitne millilitres? Thoda rukkar socho. Sahi jawab hai 1000. Baaki options kyun fit nahi hote, yeh bhi apne shabdon mein batao. Ek litre mein 1000 millilitres hote hain; bottle ki capacity isi relation se samjho. 500 mL ki do bottles milkar 1 litre banti hain. Is idea ko yaad rakhne ke liye apni notebook mein ek chhota labelled drawing banao. Jab tum apne shabdon mein samjha paate ho, tab tumne sirf answer nahi yaad kiya, balki uska reason bhi samjha. Aaj ka chhota recap: Ek litre mein 1000 millilitres hote hain; bottle ki capacity isi relation se samjho. Agli baar aas-paas ki duniya mein isi idea ka ek aur example dhoondhna.

6
